<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arab–Khazar wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 642–799</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arab–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> wars were a series of conflicts in the seventh and eighth centuries between the Khazar Khaganate and the Umayyad and early Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a> over control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>. Both sides launched major invasions through the mountain passes. The wars halted Arab expansion north of the Caucasus and established the Khazars as a major regional power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arab-khazar-wars.jpg" alt="Arab–Khazar wars" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Constantine Plakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Caucasus,_740_CE.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the <b>Arab–Khazar wars</b> of the seventh and eighth centuries the Khazars fought the Umayyad Caliphate across the Caucasus, destroying an Arab army at Marj Ardabil in 730; although Marwan ibn Muhammad's great campaign of 737 forced a temporary submission, they ultimately held the line of the Caucasus…</blockquote><a href="/empire/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate · Military</a></li></ul></section>
